{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Ends</b> Like: וקצותה את כפה — only it is from the light binyan, from possessors of heh [feminine], like מקצה רגלים. Another interpretation, and the correct one: because it clings to shame, from all the ends of the peoples." "<b>And have sinned against your soul</b> You have been in your soul."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved the unmarked biblical quotations: וקצותה את כפה = Deuteronomy 25:12; מקצה רגלים = Judges 4:10."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:14.788265297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}